# Phase 1 — Foundation

Goal: make the extension genuinely useful before adding advanced features.

### Deliverables

* ✅ VS Code extension
* ✅ Custom activity bar icon
* ✅ Tree View
* ✅ Commands
* ✅ Snippet installer
* ✅ Project generator
* ✅ Templates

Commands:

```text
Uriel: New Project

Uriel: New Character

Uriel: New Chapter

Uriel: New Scene

Uriel: New Prophecy

Uriel: Export
```

---

# Phase 2 — Codex

Instead of manually organizing notes:

```text
[[Uriel]]

[[Michael]]

[[Seven Keys]]
```

becomes

```text
Codex

Characters

Artifacts

Realms

Events

Laws

Symbols
```

generated automatically.

---

# Phase 3 — Parser

A Markdown parser that understands custom syntax like

```text
@character Uriel

@artifact CrownOfDawn

@realm First Heaven

@law Seventh Covenant

@symbol Flame
```

This is much easier to validate than relying on plain text.

---

# Phase 4 — Language Server (LSP)

The extension can provide:

* autocomplete
* hover documentation
* go to definition
* find references
* rename symbols
* diagnostics

Example:

Typing

```text
@character Ur
```

suggests

```text
Uriel
```

Hovering displays

```text
Uriel

Titles

Appears in 28 chapters

Artifacts

Relationships
```

---

# Phase 5 — Visual Graph

Think of an interactive lore map.

```text
